          %h1#20090430 2009-04-30
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    continued filling in material at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+infinity-function+theory"} geometric infinity-function theory
                    – am hoping that my co-journalists will eventually start helping me there
                %li
                  %p
                    replied to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"} David
                    at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/why+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories%3F"} why (infinity,1)-categories?
                %li
                  %p added
                  %ul
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-presheaves"} (infinity,1)-category of (infinity,1)-presheaves
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-functors"} (infinity,1)-category of (infinity,1)-functors
                    %li
                      %p
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-category of (infinity,1)-categories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"}> David
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  asked question at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/why+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories%3F"} why (infinity,1)-categories?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  added one more paragraph to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/why+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories%3F"} why (infinity,1)-categories?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"}> David
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  asked question at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  expanded
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentable (infinity,1)-category
                  by adding the theorem that every presentable
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"}> David
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  asked questions at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponential object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    started
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+simplicial+model+category"} localization of a simplicial model category
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
          %h1#20090429 2009-04-29
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  Moved the discussion about comma categories from this page to the query box at
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                %li
                  Will look at
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
                  when I get a chance.
                %li
                  Created a couple of firefox search plugins for the nLab and uploaded them to the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HowTo"} HowTo
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs
                \:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    based on
                    = succeed "\u2018s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+Skoda"} Zoran
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enhanced+triangulated+category"} enhanced triangulated category
                    I created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretriangulated+dg-category"} pretriangulated dg-category
                    and
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+complex"} twisted complex
                %li
                  %p
                    moved a bit of material from
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+infinity-stack"} derived infinity-stack
                    to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
                    and then made
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+infinity-stack"} derived infinity-stack
                    a redirect to
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
                %li
                  %p
                    finally wrote at least a blurb at
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
                    and
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaf"} (infinity,1)-sheaf
                %li
                  %p
                    created
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verdier+site"} Verdier site
                %li
                  %p
                    further fine-tuned the
                    = succeed "-review" do
                      %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0205/0205027v2.pdf"} DHI
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verdier+site"} Verdier site
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0205/0205027v2.pdf#page=29"} section 9
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0205/0205027v2.pdf#page=11"} page 11
                %li
                  %p
                    I browsed a bit through Dominic Verity’s work and created entries on
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+simplicial+set"} stratified simplicial set
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complicial+set"} complicial set
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+complicial+set"} weak complicial set
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+omega-category"} simplicial weak omega-category
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verity-Gray+tensor+product"} Verity-Gray tensor product
                    – my main motivation was the claim now recounted at
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stratified+simplicial+set"} stratified simplicial set
                    that the
                    = succeed "-nerve" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    = succeed "-categories" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ω
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Strat
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Strat
                    has a strong monoidal left adjoint
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zoran+%C5%A0koda"}> Zoran Škoda
